6h-3.744L14.77.5h3.73L15.19 8.48Zm-2.763.764a2.08 2.08 0 1 1 0 4.158 2.08 2.08 0 0 1 0-4.158Z\" fill=\"#5F01D1\"></path></svg><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"content-container svelte-17nnmqu\"><!--[-1--><!---->Yahoo<!----><!--]--></div> <!--[-1--><!--]--><!----></button><!----><!----></li></ul><!----></div><!----></div><!----><!----></div> <button class=\"ModalCloseButton svelte-t3wwh4\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close dialog\" data-trap-boundary=\"last\" data-button-style=\"flat\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 15 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" class=\"CrossIcon\" aria-label=\"Cross icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Close icon</title><path d=\"M11.782 4.032a.575.575 0 1 0-.813-.814L7.5 6.687 4.032 3.218a.575.575 0 0 0-.814.814L6.687 7.5l-3.469 3.468a.575.575 0 0 0 .814.814L7.5 8.313l3.469 3.469a.575.575 0 0 0 .813-.814L8.313 7.5l3.469-3.468Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\"></path></svg><!----><span class=\"u-visually-hidden\">Close</span></button><!----><!----></dialog><!----></div><!----> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class=\"EventModules svelte-r64kdn\"><!--[--><!--[0--><!--[9--><div class=\"EventModuleRichText svelte-6ayzyh\"><!--[0--><h2 class=\"title f-heading-4 svelte-6ayzyh\">Description</h2><!--]--> <!--[-1--><!--]--> <div class=\"RichContent f-body-3 svelte-jgfn07\"><!--[0--><!----><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#000000;--custom-color-dark:#d0d0d0\"><em>“One of the least-known masterpieces of the screen” </em></span><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">- Pauline Kael on <em>Ménilmontant</em></span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Silent Picture Show x Finch Community Cinema present: Dimitri Kirsanoff’s <em>Ménilmontant</em> (1926), a visually exquisite tour de force of the Parisian avant-garde.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Shot on the streets of the titular working-class neighbourhood for next to nothing, the film follows the fates of two orphaned sisters who, living in the wake of violent tragedy, are plagued by poverty and subject to male manipulation. Kirsanoff innovatively shuns the use of intertitles - experimenting towards a poetic, purely visual cinematic language - while lead actress Nadia Sibirskaïa (Kirsanoff’s wife and creative collaborator) is spellbinding in her naturalism.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">The mid-length feature will be complemented by Kirsanoff’s stunning lesser-known short <em>Brumes d'automne</em> (1928).</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Accompanied by live original music from acclaimed silent film pianist John Sweeney. With an introduction by event curator Ellen Cleary.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Tickets are £7, with 15% of all sales donated to MAP (Medical Aid for Palestinians).</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Doors 6:30pm, Film starts 7pm.</span></p><p><span style=\"--custom-color-light:#0b0b0b;--custom-color-dark:#cecece\">Recent digital restorations courtesy FPA Classics/Lobster Films.</span></p><!----><!--]--></div><!----></div><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></div><!--]--> <div class=\"HumanitixBannerLarge svelte-17kav4o\"><div class=\"logos svelte-17kav4o\"><span class=\"powered-by f-label-1 svelte-17kav4o\">Powered by</span> <svg class=\"HumanitixLogoSvg svelte-pxa59x\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 139 34\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><title>Humanitix logo</title><g><!--[-1--><!--]--><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M12.37 23.84c-1.06 0-1.62-.57-1.62-1.63v-2.73a.66.66 0 0 0-.72-.72H6.35a.66.66 0 0 0-.72.72v2.73c0 1.06-.56 1.63-1.62 1.63H1.62C.56 23.84 0 23.27 0 22.2v-10.2c0-1.06.56-1